{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"The reproduced deltas identify four opposing extend/retract control pairs. The body’s single marker moves in 3-cell increments, while the direct rightward route is blocked by a wall; simple extension is reversible, so the missing mechanic is anchoring/staging limbs around the barrier. I’m running a bounded BFS over only the eight observed controls, keyed on the playfield (excluding animated controls), with marker-to-target distance as the dense diagnostic."}}
